{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792481442,"nonce":"ohX1Si2VLNEL1tp1czkW2805akY=","message":"Reproduced against the pre-fix renderer from 998fa1421df975a0e9e73f6152b70b0e2fa251e1, using the corrected offscreen fixtures with a single-sampled renderer and explicit full layer opacity for effects. Four of seven pixel tests fail: blur does not reach outside content, group/nested opacity is ignored (red stays [255,0,0,255] instead of half red over blue), path-only opacity is ignored, and drop-shadow output is absent. The working source is restored after that negative control. This tests the public render_overlay_msaa entry point, not the already-fixed render_tree_with_motion branch.\n\nThe fix walks Push/Pop commands as nested ordered nodes, keeping primitive and path cursors at each boundary. It renders each layer into a tight pixel-aligned target, applies the existing native effects, and composites it at its paint position over the existing target. Path index ranges are rebased, path brush metadata is preserved, and mesh positions plus screen-space clips/gradients move into the target frame. Shared mesh and ABI clip-frame payloads are moved once per run; local polygon points and optional vertex-colour rows stay local. The batch aux_data and viewport uniforms are restored afterward. Common rounded clips are reapplied after effects.\n\nAn intermediate implementation changed mesh edge pixels by up to 36/255 when an identity filter was introduced. MSAA resolves carry premultiplied colour; composing them with SrcAlpha multiplied coverage again, and native effects expect straight colour. The new lazy alpha pass composites resolves with premultiplied blending and converts layer inputs to straight colour before effect processing. The identity filter now differs by at most 1/255; zero-radius blur is pixel-identical to the no-effect frame. Positive-radius blur still uses the existing native Kawase implementation. Whole-texture effect intermediates and blend snapshots acquire exact extents so reuse cannot stretch their pixel frame. Non-normal blends snapshot the actual target texture, including offscreen parent layers, and require COPY_SRC on that target.\n\nThe forced VB check exposed a pre-existing MSAA setup failure: the core stand-in shader declared instance attributes but its pipeline declared an empty vertex layout. The stand-in now receives the same SdfVertexInstance layout as the split MSAA pipelines. No shader-fork generation work is included.\n\nSeven offscreen GPU tests pass on Apple M1 Pro / Metal in normal SSBO, forced VB and forced DT modes (fallback capacities 1024). They cover preserved target contents, nesting and post-layer paint order, group opacity at sample counts 1 and 4, blur, rounded clipping, mesh identity/zero-blur boundaries, path-only geometry and opacity, path-local gradients, drop shadow, glow, colour filtering and Screen blending. The existing 33 display-list, two aux-routing and one clip-fill-rule GPU tests pass. GPU-free integration: 107 passed. Five new CPU tests cover range parsing, shared auxiliary data, path style/UV frames, zero blur and validation of the alpha shader. Full changed-code gate is running.\n\nRefuted setup hypotheses: an early transparent blur result came from LayerConfig::new() defaulting to opacity zero; explicit opacity 1 fixes that fixture. Readback probes showed visible input/output and matching effect texture dimensions, so the Kawase shader was not changed. Path gradients use UV/normalized parameters, not screen-space parameters; their UV frame must remain unchanged when positions move.\n\nThis slice handles native Push/Pop overlay layers; it does not add named Sample semantics or redesign the separate render_overlay entry point. The original no-glass application dispatch fix in da29258b remains in place. Actual browser WebGL2 and mobile GPU pixels remain unverified. No GPU timing benchmark was run. Processed layers add an alpha-conversion pass/intermediate; no-effect frames retain the flat MSAA route, with corrected resolve alpha handling.","files":null}]}